<title>ITALY: Italian quarterly accounts revises forecasts.</title>
<headline>Italian quarterly accounts revises forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the main data found in the Italian government's quarterly accounts which were released on Friday and include some revised forecasts -- especially for economic growth.  </p>
<p>Figures are in billion lire unless stated otherwise.</p>
<p>					 1997	 1998	 1999</p>
<p>Gross domestic product</p>
<p>    growth (GDP) (pct)	   1.2 (2.0)  2.0 (2.8)  2.5 (2.9)</p>
<p>    Inflation (pct)		2.5	  2.0	  2.0</p>
<p>    Employment growth	    0.3 (0.4)  0.6	  0.7</p>
<p>    Trend PSBR		   74,301	 n/g	  n/g</p>
<p>    Trend PSBR/GDP ratio (pct) 3.8	  n/g	  n/g</p>
<p>    Primary surplus	   115,751 (131,000) n/g    n/g</p>
<p>    Primary surplus as	   5.92	 n/g	  n/g</p>
<p>percentage of GDP</p>
<p>    Expected expenditure  1,002,046	 n/g	  n/g</p>
<p>    Expected revenues	 927,745	 n/g	  n/g</p>
<p>Note - Figures in brackets denote previously given data.</p>
<p>	   - The deficit figures show future trends based on</p>
<p>current data and do not take into account planned budget action. The government said on Friday it would introduce a mini-budget of between 15-16 trillion lire to reduce the deficit/GDP ratio to three percent this year.</p>
<p>((-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501))</p>
